      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In widening of the diagnostic to the preparation of an Intended Dynamic Group Psychotherapy was realized a common discourse at 40 juvenile patients (at an age of 17 up to 22) with the patients and their parents. Additionally neurosis screenings BFB and VFB and polarity profiles were used. Especially at the families with psychosomatic patients an externally more normal picture is given at all tests inspite of clearer inner familiar strains. This \"Pseudo-normality\" also is part of all significant concepts of psychosomatics."},
